  "description": "Tree ID 5877       An Oak tree approximately 17m in height, situated in the front garden on the norther drive entrance. Dead wood to be removed in the lower crown overhanging the pavement.\rTree ID 5878       An Austrian Pine tree approximately 16m in height, situated in the front garden midway on pavement boundary. Dead wood to be removed in the lower crown overhanging the pavement.\rTree ID 5879       A Prunus tree approximately 8m in height, situated in the front garden close to the southern boundary. Dead high stem to be removed and smaller dead wood in the lower canopy towards the property.\rTree ID 5880       A Lawson Cypress tree approximately 16m in height, situated on the north-eastern side of the property. Height to be reduced to match the line of Cypress to the left-hand side, reducing by approximately 25%. \rTree ID 5882       A Lawson Cypress tree approximately 20m in height, situated in the rear garden close to the house. Visible internal dead wood to be removed in the lower canopy. The crown also to be gently re-shaped by reducing the longest growths all over by up to 1m, importantly not revealing brown growth and retaining its natural form.\rTree ID 5883       A Sweet Chestnut tree approximately 13m in height, situated in the rear garden. One dead branch to be removed on the south-eastern axis over pathway.\rTree ID 5884       A London Plane tree. Lateral limbs on the eastern axis towards the pool to be trimmed back by up to 2m. Pruning should be targeted at natural growth points and a natural form should be retained.\rTree ID 5885       A Lawson Cypress tree approximately 14m in height, situated in the rear garden close to the property. Side stems that have fallen (x3 hanging down from main crown) to be trimmed back if needed to a side branch and the tree to have a suitable strap installed at about 7m from ground level to support all stems together.\r",
